<h2>Segment 260 &mdash; consequences for other sense consciousnesses</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s260S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s260w1">&#x27;o na</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w2">mi</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w3">mig <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w4">shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w5">tshad ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w6">ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w7">yin</span> par thal, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w8">mi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w9">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w10">&#x27;bring po</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w11">dbang gis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w12">chur</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w13">mthong ba</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w14">tsam</span> yin pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w15">phyir</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s260w16">gzhan yang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w17">mi</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w18">ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260r1">yin</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w19">&#x27;gro ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w20">rgyud</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w21"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w22">lus</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w23">shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w24">tshad ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w25">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w26"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w27">nyan</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w28">shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w29">tshad ma</span> yang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w30">med</span> par <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w31">thal</span>, de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w32">rgyud</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w33">mig <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w34">shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w35">tshad ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w36">med</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w37">phyir</span>, der thal, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s260w38">khyod kyi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w39"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w40">rtsa ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w41">dam bca&#x27;</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w42">&#x27;thad pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w43">phyir</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w44">&#x27;dod</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w45">na</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s260S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s260w1">Well then</span>, according to you, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w3">visual <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w4">consciousness</span></span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w2">human</span> would<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w6">n&#x27;t</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w7">be</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w5">valid perception</span> either. <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w15">Because</span> isn&#x27;t it true that the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w8">human</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w13">sees</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w12">water</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w14">only</span> because his <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w9">karma</span> (which in this case is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w10">halfway</span> between the good and the bad just mentioned) <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w11">forces</span> him to? <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s260w16">Moreover</span>, aren&#x27;t you <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w31">implying</span> then that there is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w30">no</span> such thing as a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w24">valid</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w21"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w22">tactile</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w23">consciousness</span></span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w25">or</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w29">valid</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w26"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w27">auditory</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w28">consciousness</span></span>, in the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w20">mental stream</span> of any <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w19">being</span> who <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260r1">is</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w18">not</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w17">human</span>? <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w37">Because</span> aren&#x27;t you saying that there&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w36">no</span> such thing as a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w35">valid</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w33">visual <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w34">consciousness</span></span> in the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w32">mental stream</span> of any such being? Certainly you are, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w43">for</span> you believe <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s260w38">your</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w39"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w40">original</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s260w41">position</span></span> to be <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w42">correct</span>. And <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s260w45">suppose</span> now that you do <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s260w44">agree</span> that such beings can have no such valid consciousnesses.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, reconciled from independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals; not human-approved. Four tshad ma occurrences are retained: valid perception first, then valid for tactile, auditory and visual consciousness. The English-first original note's three count is superseded here; the frozen original is preserved. All three mi/human and both rgyud/mental stream occurrences have separate ranges. The first ma owns only the n't in wouldn't, with subword true; later rhetorical isn't/aren't are not additional source negatives. The copular yin words own be and the is in who is not a human at d5. 'bring po owns halfway; the comparison to good and bad is supplied from context. dbang gis owns forces, leaving him to supplied. chur/water keeps the entire inflected syllable. The second thal owns only implying; supplied address, auxiliaries and rhetorical framing stay unwrapped. Initial thal, der thal, de'i, yang and unselected case/reason framing are omitted where their English realization is distributed. khyod kyi owns your as a possessive phrase at d3; rtsa ba'i dam bca' is the established original position compound with tighter original/position members. The final 'dod/agree and na/suppose retain the acceptance branch; the expanded final valid consciousnesses is unwrapped. No null substitutes for unresolved distribution, and all original source wording is preserved.</div>
